            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>Added</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>The preview panel now tells you as much as Finder's Get Info.</b> For folders and files without a visual preview, the info panel shows the created and last-opened dates, any Finder tags (as color chips), and — for folders — how many items they hold, alongside the name, kind, size, and modified date it already showed. Fields with no value are simply left out, so nothing reads as empty or "Unknown". Free for everyone.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Google Drive and other cloud files no longer show as 0 KB.</b> Online-only documents (Google Docs, Sheets, Slides and similar placeholder files) keep no data on disk, so their size read as zero; Explorer now shows their real size, matching Finder.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
